  "blog.beginner.upload.title": "1. Uploading Your Image",
  "blog.dithering.balancing.desc": "The key to effective dithering is finding the right balance. Too much dithering can make an image look noisy, while too little can result in harsh color banding. Experimentation is crucial to achieve the desired effect for your Wplace pixel art.",
  "blog.dithering.balancing.title": "Balancing Detail and Aesthetic",
  "blog.dithering.closing": "Master dithering to add depth and richness to your Wplace pixel art!",
  "blog.dithering.floyd_steinberg.application": "<strong>Application:</strong> Our Wplace Paint Tool offers an option to enable Floyd-Steinberg dithering for enhanced color blending.",
  "blog.dithering.floyd_steinberg.benefits": "<strong>Benefits:</strong> Produces excellent results with minimal banding, ideal for achieving smooth transitions with limited palettes.",
  "blog.dithering.floyd_steinberg.desc": "Floyd-Steinberg is one of the most common and effective dithering algorithms. It works by propagating the quantization error of each pixel to its neighboring pixels, creating a smooth and natural-looking gradient.",
  "blog.dithering.floyd_steinberg.how_it_works": "<strong>How it Works:</strong> Error is distributed to the right, bottom-left, bottom, and bottom-right pixels.",
  "blog.dithering.floyd_steinberg.title": "Floyd-Steinberg Dithering",
  "blog.dithering.intro": "Dithering is a powerful technique in pixel art that allows you to create the illusion of more colors and smoother gradients than your limited palette actually provides. This guide will explore the art and science behind dithering, focusing on its application in Wplace pixel art.",
  "blog.dithering.other_techniques.desc": "While Floyd-Steinberg is popular, other methods exist:",
  "blog.dithering.other_techniques.ordered": "<strong>Ordered Dithering:</strong> Uses a fixed pattern to determine where to place pixels. Can create a more stylized, grainy look.",
  "blog.dithering.other_techniques.random": "<strong>Random Dithering:</strong> Simply adds random noise. Less effective at smoothing gradients but can be used for specific artistic effects.",
  "blog.dithering.other_techniques.title": "Other Dithering Techniques",
  "blog.dithering.tips.consider_palette": "<strong>Consider the Palette:</strong> Dithering is most useful when working with very limited color palettes.",
  "blog.dithering.tips.preview": "<strong>Preview Regularly:</strong> Always check your dithered image in the Wplace Paint Tool's preview to ensure it meets your expectations.",
  "blog.dithering.tips.subtle": "<strong>Subtle is Key:</strong> Often, a subtle application of dithering is more effective than an aggressive one.",
  "blog.dithering.tips.title": "Tips for Using Dithering",
  "blog.dithering.title": "Enhancing Detail: The Art and Science of Dithering in Pixel Art",
  "blog.dithering.what_is.desc": "Dithering is the intentional application of noise to randomize quantization error, preventing large-scale patterns such as color banding. In pixel art, it's used to simulate colors not available in the palette by strategically placing pixels of available colors.",
  "blog.dithering.what_is.title": "What is Dithering?",
  "blog.minread": "min read",
  "blog.palette.advanced.desc": "Beyond simply picking colors, consider these advanced techniques:",
  "blog.palette.advanced.hue_shifting": "<strong>Hue Shifting:</strong> Instead of just darkening or lightening a color, subtly shift its hue as you move from light to shadow. This adds vibrancy and realism.",
  "blog.palette.advanced.limited": "<strong>Limited Palettes:</strong> Challenge yourself to create compelling art with a very small subset of colors. This forces creativity and strengthens your understanding of color value.",
  "blog.palette.advanced.ramps": "<strong>Color Ramps:</strong> Create smooth transitions between colors for shading and highlights. Even with a limited palette, effective ramps can add significant depth.",
  "blog.palette.advanced.title": "2. Advanced Color Selection Techniques",
  "blog.palette.closing": "Unleash the power of color in your Wplace creations!",
  "blog.palette.customizing.contextual": "<strong>Contextual Application:</strong> The same color can appear different depending on the colors surrounding it. Use this optical illusion to your advantage.",
  "blog.palette.customizing.desc": "While the Wplace palette is fixed, you can still customize your approach:",
  "blog.palette.customizing.precomputation": "<strong>Pre-computation:</strong> Use external tools or your own Wplace Paint Tool experiments to pre-determine which Wplace colors best represent your desired hues.",
  "blog.palette.customizing.title": "3. Customizing and Adapting Palettes",
  "blog.palette.harmony.analogous": "<strong>Analogous Colors:</strong> Colors next to each other on the color wheel create a sense of calm and unity.",
  "blog.palette.harmony.complementary": "<strong>Complementary Colors:</strong> Colors opposite each other create strong contrast and visual excitement.",
  "blog.palette.harmony.desc": "Color harmony isn't just about aesthetics; it's about conveying emotion and guiding the viewer's eye:",
  "blog.palette.harmony.monochromatic": "<strong>Monochromatic Schemes:</strong> Using different shades and tints of a single color can create sophisticated and cohesive artwork.",
  "blog.palette.harmony.title": "4. Achieving Color Harmony and Mood",
  "blog.palette.intro": "In pixel art, the color palette is the foundation of your artwork. A well-chosen palette can make your art cohesive, vibrant, and visually appealing, while a poorly chosen one can make even the best pixel work look amateurish. This guide will teach you the essential strategies for creating and using color palettes effectively.",
  "blog.palette.tips.less_is_more": "<strong>Less is More:</strong> Often, a well-chosen limited palette is more impactful than a sprawling one.",
  "blog.palette.tips.study_masters": "<strong>Study Masters:</strong> Analyze the color choices of renowned pixel artists for inspiration and learning.",
  "blog.palette.tips.test_canvas": "<strong>Test on Canvas:</strong> Always preview your pixel art on the Wplace canvas to see how colors render in the actual environment.",
  "blog.palette.tips.title": "Tips for Effective Color Use",
  "blog.palette.title": "Color Palette Strategies for Pixel Art: Mastering the Foundation of Your Artwork",
  "blog.palette.understanding.desc": "A color palette is a limited set of colors used consistently throughout your artwork. Constraints breed creativity, and working with a limited palette forces you to be more intentional with your color choices.",
