  "blog.resampling.nearest.cons": "<strong>Cons:</strong> Can create jagged lines and \"staircasing\" effects if not used carefully, especially when downscaling.",
  "blog.resampling.nearest.desc": "Nearest Neighbor is the simplest and often preferred method for pixel art. It works by simply duplicating or removing pixels without any interpolation. This results in sharp, blocky edges, preserving the distinct pixelated look.",
  "blog.resampling.nearest.pros": "<strong>Pros:</strong> Maintains pixel crispness, no blurring, ideal for upscaling pixel art.",
